              <h3 class="text-lg font-bold text-red-900 mt-0 mb-2">Buying a Mower Sized for a Bigger Yard</h3>
              <p class="text-gray-700 text-sm m-0">
                A wide, heavy, self-propelled mower designed for a half-acre-plus property is genuinely harder to use on a small, obstacle-filled lawn than a compact, purpose-built small-yard mower. Bigger specs don't automatically mean a better fit — match the mower to the actual shape and size of your lawn, not to the biggest number on the spec sheet.
              </p>
            </div>
            <div class="bg-red-50 border border-red-100 rounded-2xl p-6">
              <h3 class="text-lg font-bold text-red-900 mt-0 mb-2">Choosing a Reel Mower for an Inconsistent Mowing Schedule</h3>
              <p class="text-gray-700 text-sm m-0">
                Reel mowers reward discipline and punish neglect. If your actual mowing habit is closer to every two or three weeks than every week, a reel mower will constantly struggle and frustrate you. Be honest about your actual schedule before choosing a mower type that depends on a strict one.
              </p>
